  animalName: Tyrannosaurus Rex
  scientificName: Tyrannosaurus rex
  classification: Apex Carnivore (Meat Eater)
  era: Late Cretaceous (~68 - 66 Million Years Ago)
  averageLength: 12.3 meters (40 ft)
  averageWeight: 8,400 kg (8.4 metric tons)
  description: Tyrannosaurus Rex stands as one of the most iconic and terrifying
    land predators to ever walk the Earth, dominating the western North American
    landscape during the Late Cretaceous period roughly 68 to 66 million years ago.
    Reaching lengths of up to 40 feet and weighing around 8 metric tons, this massive
    bipedal carnivore possessed a heavily reinforced skull housing a devastating
    bite force capable of crushing bone. Its mouth was packed with serrated, banana-sized
    teeth up to 12 inches long, which allowed it to easily tear through the tough
    hides of contemporary herbivores. Supported by immensely powerful hind legs that
    provided surprising agility for its scale, T. rex balanced its body with a thick,
    heavy tail, using its advanced binocular vision and exceptionally sharp sense
    of smell to track down prey or locate carcasses across vast distances.
  funFact: T-Rex possessed the strongest bite force of any terrestrial animal in
    Earth's history - over 12,800 pounds of force, easily crushing bone!
